WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.760
Don't "hulk out," Marvel fans Mark Ruffalo
isn't actually being fired from the MCU.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.360
But Avengers 4 directors the Russo Brothers
are doing an admirable job keeping a running

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.920
gag about Ruffalo's termination going.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.860
It all started back in October, when Ruffalo
apparently slipped up and stated out loud

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.500
the actual title of Avengers 4 on the Tonight
Show Starring Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.300
The Russo Brothers and the bigwigs at Marvel
have kept the title top secret, since it's

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.260
reportedly a spoiler for the preceding film,
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.900
"I think I can probably tell you that."

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.620
"Really?"

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.800
"I think it's already out there.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.440
The title of the next Avengers movie is [BLEEP]."

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.180
The Hulk actor took to Twitter following the
taping to send a tweet to Fallon, asking the

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.600
late-night host to have his team edit the
episode and save his hide.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.140
"@JimmyFallon , I trust that you will cut
my spoiler slip on the show tonight.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.900
That was 'off the record' homey.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.920
Please don't get me in trouble with Marvel
(Barry) again.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:57.700
DM me back.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.200
M."

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.920
The supposed spoiler was ultimately censored
and a black bar was placed over Ruffalo's

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:08.310
mouth in the cut that aired on television,
but Joe Russo and his co-directing bro Anthony,

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.360
along with Ruffalo, decided to keep the gag
alive online.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.360
Ten days after Ruffalo's apparent misstep,
the Russos uploaded a cryptic photo to their

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.360
joint Twitter page, celebrating the end of
filming on Avengers 4.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.580
Ruffalo responded to their tweet, poking fun
at how unfair it is that they can share anything

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.760
they want but he got fired for dropping Avengers
4 info.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.000
"You fired me for a measly slip of the title?

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:32.620
Spoiler alert!"

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.820
The Russo Brothers then quipped back,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.400
"You're still fired, Mark."

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.740
During an Instagram Q&amp;A session held on Thursday,
November 8th at his new bar Duello in Los

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:46.619
Angeles, Joe Russo was asked how he deals
with spoiler-happy actors like Ruffalo.

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:49.799
His bartender asks, "Didn't you fire Mark
Ruffalo?"

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.480
To which Russo replies, "Yes, we fired [him].

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.200
Mark's fired."

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.940
You have to hand it to them: Their commitment
to the joke is impressive!

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:02.040
As for the title that Ruffalo supposedly let
slip on The Tonight Show, one Marvel fan did

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:07.640
some fancy audio-editing and revealed that
Ruffalo told Fallon that Avengers 4 is titled

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.430
The Last Avenger — which would neatly connect
to Captain America: The First Avenger from

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.140
2011.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.920
"The Last Avenger."

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.040
"The Last Avenger."

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.840
But don't get too excited.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.859
Someone who was in attendance at the Tonight
Show taping shot down the speculation, stating

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:27.819
that the whole thing was "a bit" and that
Ruffalo told the audience during a commercial

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.950
break that what he said wasn't true.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:30.940
"Don't bother!

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.980
I was there, after they went to commercial
he said none of it actually happens.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.949
He said something about Bruce finally becoming
the Hulk again (which I hope will happen in

00:02:38.949 --> 00:02:40.860
a4!!) having to do with some lava.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.640
But yeah it was definitely a bit."

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.989
So while Ruffalo and the Russos have done
excellent work whipping Marvel fans into a

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:51.469
frenzy with their title-teasing antics, it
looks like we'll all have to wait just a little

00:02:51.469 --> 00:02:54.329
longer to learn the true title of Avengers
4.

00:02:54.329 --> 00:02:58.760
The studio is reportedly holding off on revealing
it until the end of 2018.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.640
As for the film itself, Joe Russo revealed
in his Instagram Q&amp;A that the stakes will

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:09.099
be way higher in Avengers 4, as expected,
and the epic Infinity War follow-up is currently

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:13.699
only half edited, with a ton of painstaking
effects work left to complete.

00:03:13.699 --> 00:03:19.989
See the final product when the still-totally-untitled
Avengers 4 hits theaters May 3rd, 2019.

